##!
# Missionaries and cannibals, with weather.
#
# Three missionaries and three cannibals cross a river in a boat. If cannibals ever outnumber
# missionaries on a bank (with any missionaries there), the trip fails, so the agent never makes
# that crossing. The twist: the river reports its weather on the input link each decision.
#
#   ^io.input-link.river.current calm | strong   strong current: the boat holds one, not two
#   ^io.input-link.river.storm no | yes          storm: nobody crosses
#   ^io.input-link.river.time <n>                the river's clock, one tick per decision
#
# The weather comes from a recording, so a run replays exactly:
#
#   rusty-soar-cli trace examples/river-crossing/load.soar --input examples/river-crossing/weather.rec
#
# The agent starts over each time everyone is across, and reinforcement learning (one
# Q-value per bank, boat side and move, generated by a macro) learns which crossings get
# everyone over soonest. Near the end the recording turns learning and exploration off.

source settings.soar
source crossing.soar
source learning.soar
